==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Eyewaltz CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Nameless Eyewaltz CC''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Similarly to the Normal and Evolved Forms of [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Keiji]], Eyewaltz is a mid-ranger with mediocre base stats. Eyewaltz has higher base stats, though has a longer recharge time. While Keiji gets an increase in DPS through strengthen, Eyewaltz relies on random chance from [[Savage Blow|Savage Blows]] and does either 76.5k or 25.5k. Though his recharge time is longer than Keiji, his cost is similar and he still has a fast recharge. Unlike Keiji, Eyewaltz is not a tanky unit (though he still has above average health for an Uber) and its chance to [[Survive]] a lethal strike effectively gives him four knockbacks.

His [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] is nice, since he can outrange most [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave enemies]]. It means he can be used against [[Dober P.D]] and [[Hermit Cat (Enemy)|Hermit Cat]], and in wave stages in general, especially since they are stingy with money.

Overall, he is a good mid-ranger with decent generalist usage and wave immunity.

==='''True Form'''===
Although a rather simple change on the surface, Eyewaltz's True Form brings massive improvements to the table. Most noticeably, because of his Wave Attack, his overall average DPS doubles to a massive 14k, which is huge for a pure generalist unit. At level 50, Nameless Eyewaltz has on average ''22.4k dps''; easily able to shred through countless enemies. Also important to mention is that his [[Wave Attack]] gives him pierce. He can reach up to 532.5 range with 7k dps (11k dps at Lv.50). While his damage is equal to an on-level Slime Cat (which has longer Waves), Eyewaltz is much more sustainable and proves to be a consistent answer versus midrangers and backliners. Other than damage, all of Eyewaltz's previous qualities still apply. However, it is necessary to note that due to Eyewaltz relying on Savage Blows and Waves, damage output is not always consistent.

Overall, Eyewaltz's True Form makes him one of the current best collab ubers.

==='''Talents'''===
Even given the fact Eyewaltz did not get Attack Up talents, his Talent selection is still extremely strong and worth investing into.

His first talent is '''Savage Blow''', increasing the chance of it occuring up to 25%. When a Savage Blow lands, Eyewaltz is capable of dealing some ridiculous damage, up to 243,000 damage at Lv.50 assuming both the Wave and the initial hit lands on the same enemy. With more consistent Savage Blows, you can expect to see a Savage Blow around once every 20 seconds he's alive. With this Talent fully maxed out, Eyewaltz's true DPS inflates to over ''25k at level 50''. Absolutely get this Talent before anything else here.

Eyewaltz also gets two immunities and a Resist talent: '''[[Immune to Weaken|Weaken Immune]]''', '''[[Immune to Knockback|Knockback Immune]]''', and '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Slow Resist]]'''. Weaken Immunity is more relevant for matchups like [[Winged Pigge]] and [[Calamary]], so they're not a bad decision, while Knockback Immunity is pretty bad given that Eyewaltz does want to resposition. There are little relevant situations where Eyewaltz not getting knocked back is beneficial, whereas there are many more scenarios in which he would take a damage knockback anyway. Make of that what you will. Slow Resist is a Resist talent and has nearly no relevant matchups. Don't buy it.

Finally, Eyewaltz gets '''Defense Up'''. Giving him more health isn't a bad idea, but it is of very low priority as he works fine without it.

==='''Orb'''===
Any attack or Defense Orb works wonders on Eyewaltz. For Ability Orbs, Berserker Orb is his best option by far, though Colossus Slayer and Dodge Attack can be used effectively on him since he's able to be semi-quickly cycled.

